# Frontend Architecture Rules

## Overview

Strict separation: **components** consume **hooks**; **hooks/data** call **`config/api`**; **services** stay framework-agnostic. **Apps** (`apps/web`, `apps/mobile`) are thin composition layers; **feature UI** lives in **`packages/features/<feature>/`**. Full import matrix and layer write-ups: [documentation/client/layered-architecture-imports.md](../../../documentation/client/layered-architecture-imports.md).

**Also see:** `ui-components.mdc`, `platform-file-extensions.mdc`, `openapi-types.mdc`, `Client/ARCHITECTURE.md`, [workspace-first-architecture.md](../../../documentation/client/workspace-first-architecture.md).

## React and JSX placement

| Location | JSX / UI | Hooks (.ts) |
| -------- | -------- | ------------- |
| `Client/apps/web/` | Yes — thin pages, layouts, composition | Rare; prefer `packages/hooks` |
| `Client/apps/mobile/` | Yes — thin screens (see platform-file-extensions) | Same |
| `Client/packages/features/*/` | Yes — feature components | Feature-local `hooks/` as needed |
| `Client/packages/ui/` | Yes — design system | N/A |
| `Client/packages/contexts/` | Providers only | N/A |
| `Client/packages/hooks/` | **No** — `.ts` only | Yes |
| `Client/packages/services/`, `config/` (except query setup), `store/`, `schemas/`, `utils/` | **No** | No (except `config/query`) |

Do not put standalone `.ts` business logic or utilities under `apps/web/components/` or `apps/web/features/` — use `packages/utils/`, `packages/hooks/`, or `packages/schemas/`.

## Dependency flow

```text
Feature UI (packages/features/, apps) → hooks (packages/hooks/) → config/api → HTTP/security utils
Services (packages/services/) → config/api only (no React, no hooks)
```

Features must not bypass adapters/primitives to poke at raw DOM or RN APIs when a shared primitive exists (see `cross-platform-component-reuse.mdc`).

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Page composes feature UI and uses a shared data hook
// apps/web/pages/SavedPage.tsx
import { useSavedHomesData } from "packages/hooks/data/useSavedHomesData";
import { SavedHomesPanel } from "packages/features/saved/components/SavedHomesPanel";

export default function SavedPage() {
  const { savedHomes } = useSavedHomesData();
  return <SavedHomesPanel homes={savedHomes} />;
}

// ❌ WRONG: UI imports API client directly
import { userApi } from "packages/config/api/user"; // FORBIDDEN in components

// ❌ WRONG: Hook file contains JSX
// packages/hooks/data/useFoo.tsx with <div /> — FORBIDDEN; use .ts only
```

## Enforcement checklist

1. UI and feature components: no direct `config/api/*` or business `services/*` imports.
2. `hooks/data/*`: only `config/api/*`, not `services/agent`-style classes.
3. New shared logic: `packages/utils` or `packages/hooks`, not `apps/web/features` as raw `.ts` dumping ground.

